cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Exploding-Sandpiles: a Lean 4 formalization of A shape theorem for exploding sandpiles"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the paper "A shape theorem
  for exploding sandpiles" (Bou-Rabee): the limit shape theorem, the convergence
  of the rescaled arrival times, the explosion criterion for product backgrounds,
  the convergence of the exploding sandpile under general hypotheses, and
  explosive backgrounds without a limit shape (Theorems 1.2, 1.3, 1.4, 5.1 and
  6.1), together with every lemma and proposition that the paper proves.  The
  results are proved from the seven results the paper cites from the literature,
  which enter as explicit hypotheses; six of the seven are also proved in the
  repository, and only the chemical-distance bound of Antal and Pisztora is
  assumed.  The library contains
  no sorry and no custom axiom; the Mathlib-only comparator challenge for the
  limit shape theorem contains one intentional statement-level sorry whose
  completed solution is checked separately.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Abelian sandpile
  - exploding sandpile
  - limit shape
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
# TODO(author): add a Zenodo DOI once an archived release is minted.
